  "id": "conceptual-replication",
  "term": "conceptual replication",
  "definition": "Conceptual replication is a follow-up study that tests the same underlying idea or effect as an earlier study but uses different tasks or measures. In the source example, the same power-performance question was examined with new performance tasks rather than repeating the original task exactly.",
